X:1
T:Que Sera, Sera
C:Jay Livingston and Ray Evans, 1956
N:Best-effort version, not verified against a second source. Melody is the
N:upper voice of a choral arrangement MIDI (hamienet.com), moved up a whole
N:step so the lowest note is not below C4. Bars 1-16 are the first section,
N:bars 17-36 the section that follows it in the arrangement (before its key
N:change). Chords come from that arrangement's piano and bass. The lead line
N:is least certain in bars 10-15 and 17-36, where the voices split.
